 {
  "object": "block",
  "id": "38894183-19f3-804f-b2b3-eacc5bd020c5",
  "parent": {
   "type": "page_id",
   "page_id": "38894183-19f3-8054-8779-f668dd242f1e"
  },
  "created_time": "2026-06-23T18:14:00.000Z",
  "last_edited_time": "2026-07-02T09:30:00.000Z",
  "created_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "815cd27b-5ca8-4b38-8784-7f2f8565f656"
  },
  "last_edited_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "37c94183-19f3-81a8-88c7-002741ff0f4c"
  },
  "has_children": false,
  "in_trash": false,
  "type": "paragraph",
  "paragraph": {
   "rich_text": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": {
      "content": "A week into Cascadia's soft launch, Emil brings Sofia a specific complaint from Lena: some customer messages just hang. No error message, no failure notification \u2014 the workflow starts, an agent goes off to look something up, and nothing ever comes back. Sofia opens the logs and sees the same pattern each time: one component was waiting for another that never responded, and the whole workflow got stuck on that wait. Timeouts are how orchestrated systems refuse to wait forever. This lesson explains why waits happen, why leaving them uncapped is dangerous, and how timeouts protect the whole workflow when one component slows down.",
      "link": null
     },
     "annotations": {
      "bold": false,
      "italic": false,
      "strikethrough": false,
      "underline": false,
      "code": false,
      "color": "default"
     },
     "plain_text": "A week into Cascadia's soft launch, Emil brings Sofia a specific complaint from Lena: some customer messages just hang. No error message, no failure notification \u2014 the workflow starts, an agent goes off to look something up, and nothing ever comes back. Sofia opens the logs and sees the same pattern each time: one component was waiting for another that never responded, and the whole workflow got stuck on that wait. Timeouts are how orchestrated systems refuse to wait forever. This lesson explains why waits happen, why leaving them uncapped is dangerous, and how timeouts protect the whole workflow when one component slows down.",
     "href": null
    }
   ],
   "icon": null,
   "color": "default"
  },
  "archived": false
 },
